	(text "LEVEL SHIFTER vs DOTSTAR RATE - checked, it works\n(design review asked).\nU7 = SN74AHCT125 quad buffer, tpd ~6-10 ns at 5V,\nrated well past 100 MHz. The design doc prescales\nthe DotStar SPI to 7.815 Mbit/s (12 MHz is the\nAPA102 ceiling).\n   one bit at 7.815 MHz = 128 ns\n   tpd 10 ns = 8% of a bit\n   -> nowhere near the limit. VERDICT: fine.\n\n3.3V INPUT SIDE - why the part is AHCT, not AHC:\n   AHCT has TTL input thresholds, VIH = 2.0 V max,\n   so a 3.3 V CMOS output clears it by 1.3 V.\n   Plain AHC is CMOS-threshold, VIH = 0.7 x 5 =\n   3.5 V, which a 3.3 V output can NEVER reach.\n   AHC here would half-work and glitch. Do not\n   substitute.\nU7 runs from +5V (pin 14) so its outputs swing 5 V.\n2 of the 4 buffers are used:\n   pin2 -> pin3 = CLK,  pin5 -> pin6 = DATA\nThe 2 spare buffers have their INPUTS tied to +5V\n(pins 10, 13) so nothing floats; their outputs\n(pins 8, 11) are left open. All four ~OE pins\n(1, 4, 9, 12) are tied to GND = enabled.\n\nDECOUPLING (\"maybe more caps to the DotStars\")\n   C45 100nF at U7's supply pin.\n   C40-C44 100nF, one per LED - D3..D7 left to right.\n   C51 22uF NEW bulk reservoir at the head of the\n       string. Five APA102-2020 at full white draw\n       ~300 mA and switch it at the frame rate;\n       100nF parts cannot supply that, and the\n       nearest bulk (C3, 22uF) is on the power sheet.\nLayout: C40-C44 are NOT interchangeable - each sits\nbeside its own LED. The five LEDs must be placed in\nthe 5-dot pattern of the robot shell (design doc)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 297.18 252.73 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "7a9d5a69-dbbf-4626-8f5c-08a0c7fe09d3")
	)
